    "text": "We say that a graph is $4$-chromatic critical if it has chromatic number $4$, and removing any edge decreases the chromatic number to $3$.\nIs there, for arbitrarily large $n$, a $4$-chromatic critical graph on $n$ vertices with minimum degree $\\gg n$?",
